     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	NIEC institutional structure strengthened including NIEC presence in the FMS
&#x2022;	NIEC operational capacity development and training plan developed to conduct operations both at HQ and field level. 

&#x2022;	NIEC Voter Education operational plan for the electoral process including Voter Registration Phase fully developed and shared with NIEC Field Offices and stakeholders.                         
&#x2022;	Production of Voter Education Materials for the electoral process including Voter Registration Process developed Public Service Announcements for TV and for Radio produced and broadcast on main TV and radio stations throughout the country. Printed material targeting women&#x2019;s participation in the Voter Registration process are produced and disseminated through NIEC Field Offices.
&#x2022;	Develop and implement inclusive NIEC external relations strategy with key stakeholders, such as political parties, universities, CSOs including women and youth associations, media. 
&#x2022;	Political Parties enabled to achieve official registration by NIEC. 
&#x2022;	Political Parties nominate candidates for elections. 
&#x2022;	NIEC decides on VR methodology and agreed by key stakeholders; NIEC VR plan completed including specific measures to enhance women&#x2019;s registration and polling.
&#x2022;	NIEC VR plan fully developed and implemented.
&#x2022;	Voter registration/polling centres in identified secured areas vetted by security forces 
&#x2022;	NIEC successfully supported in the procurement of necessary voter registration (and polling) material and equipment
&#x2022;	NIEC Data Centre to be completed by second quarter 2020.
&#x2022;	Construction on central warehouse, Electoral Dispute Resolution Mechanism building and enhanced security protection for the NIEC compound to begin in second quarter of 2020. 
&#x2022;	Electoral Law adopted by Parliament, signed by the President, published in Official Gazette and enforced
&#x2022;	Amendments to Political Parties Law adopted by Parliament.
&#x2022;	Advice provided to NIEC, Legislative Committee, Members of both Houses of Parliament on revisions required to the legal provisions of the electoral bill, including the Electoral Dispute Resolution Mechanism. 
&#x2022;	Clarifications and gaps in the Electoral Law addressed by the Ad Hoc Joint Parliamentary Committee
&#x2022;	Regulations and procedures drafted by NIEC based on the Electoral Law.
&#x2022;	Project unqualified audit report
&#x2022;	Thorough implementation of the agreed Work Plan and responsible resource management
&#x2022;	Support services for electoral activities are provided in a timely and qualitative manner.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Capacity building support was provided in line with the strategic plan. IESG has supported NIEC in establishing its field offices in each of the FMS and Banadir (except Somaliland) 
- NIEC&#x2019;s civic education campaign on the electoral process reached most of its intended audience across the country.
- A draft voter registration plan and other key logistic documents were developed. 
- Completion of the construction of the NIEC&#x2019;s new data center and handed it over to NIEC. 
 - Electoral law and Amendments to the Political Parties law have been approved.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	NIEC institutional structure strengthened including NIEC presence in the FMS
2.	NIEC capacity development and training plan developed, and implementation commenced                              
3.	At least 30% of women as UN-supported national advisors                               
4.	Development of NIEC 5-year strategic plan (2022-2026)                        
5.	NIEC Regional offices well-functioning.
6.	NIEC public awareness strategy plan developed.                                                                     
7.	Development and implementation of an inclusive NIEC external relations strategy with key stakeholders, including political parties, CSOs and Media.
8.	NIEC Public Outreach institutional structure strengthened including NIEC field offices at the FMS level.
9.	Completion of NIEC office infrastructure and security enhancements
10. Sound implementation of the agreed Work Plan and responsible resource management
11. Electoral committees capacitated to implement Indirect elections
12. Gender quota implemented for women&#x2019;s seats in both Houses of Parliament</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-	The NIEC held a three-day all staff reflection retreat in Mogadishu between 24-26 January 2021. The retreat provided an opportunity for the NIEC to primarily review its internal functioning, assess the Commission&#x2019;s accomplishments as an organization as well as identify challenges and the lessons learnt since the NIEC was established in 2015. The exercise was broadly based on the NIEC&#x2019;s five-year Strategic Plan 2017-2021 which guided the overall agenda of the retreat with particular emphasis on NIEC&#x2019;s internal organizational functions. Staff and the NIEC Commissioners participated in the retreat. A draft report including recommendations and follow up actions was prepared and approved by the Board of Commissioners. 
-	NIEC conducted several capacity building workshops both internally and with the support of IESG to help bolster knowledge and skills of its staff. Institutional capacity development is essential in ensuring a strong and independent electoral management body. Many trainings were conducted virtually as COVID-19 has been increasing in Somalia since December 2020.
-	To date, the Office of the Political Parties Registrar has provided temporary registration to 110 Political parties. IESG, in collaboration with the Office of the Political Parties Registrar (OPPR), are working on developing software for a database to register political parties.  
-	On 27th January, NIEC Board of Commissioners, Directors and Senior advisors met with IESG officials to discuss the way forward on developing an election roadmap. Universal suffrage elections are scheduled to be held in 2024/2025.  
-	The NIEC conducted an internal strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats (SWOT) exercise as part of their institutional self-appraisal which will inform the development of new Strategic Plan for 2022-2026 during the third quarter of 2021.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	NIEC institutional structure strengthened including NIEC presence in the FMS
2.	NIEC capacity development and training plan developed, and implementation commenced                              
3.	At least 30% of women as UN-supported national advisors                               
4.	Development of NIEC 5-year strategic plan (2022-2026)                        
5.	NIEC Regional offices well-functioning.
6.	NIEC public awareness strategy plan developed.                                                                     
7.	Development and implementation of an inclusive NIEC external relations strategy with key stakeholders, including political parties, CSOs and Media.
8.	NIEC Public Outreach institutional structure strengthened including NIEC field offices at the FMS level.
9.	Sound implementation of the agreed Work Plan and responsible resource management
10.	Electoral ad-hoc committees capacitated to implement Indirect elections
11.	Gender quota implemented for women&#x2019;s seats in both Houses of Parliament</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Technical assistance was provided to the NIEC in the implementation of its new 5-year Strategic Plan (2022 -2026) and finalizing the tentative roadmap for universal suffrage elections in 2026. 
2.	Support was focused on day-to-day NIEC operations, capacity building at HQ and local levels (HR, performance appraisal, reporting, procurement and financial management), legal support for electoral review, and logistics (process of handing over the assets procured during the indirect elections to the NIEC possession). 
3.	A set of NIEC visibility and public outreach materials have been developed for further use in the civic education campaigns. 
4.	Support was provided to the NIEC in 2022 in drafting regulations on Voter Registration and Secondary Legislation, Policies and Guidelines.
5.	Support was provided to the NIEC to develop an action plan for the institutions gender equality strategy and a new performance management plan for the staff of the Election Commission. Under the action plan, the focus is on promoting gender equality and women&#x2019;s participation in the administration and management of electoral processes as well as political decision-making.
6.	UNDP continued to support political reconciliation through facilitating consensus between FGS and the FMS on the completion of the indirect process and advocating for the 30% womens quota in parliament. 
7.	The support was provided to the Office of Prime Minister and ad-hoc electoral committees (FEIT, SEITs and EDRC) to conduct the indirect electoral process in line with the national procurement regulations. Indirect elections were completed in May 2022. The new government was formed in August 2022. 
8.	UN continued expanding and strengthening its electoral assistance at the FMS level. The support to the Transitional Puntland Electoral Commission has been initiated to conduct the 2022- 2023 local elections process, by providing technical expertise and continuous finance management capacity building.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
